<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.4.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00907</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.4.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>ccdfa7b6-f7f9-48ac-8e68-5307c03d56db</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">
    <para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<!--Do not edit this div tag.  It must surround the interaction block-->
<section id="sect-00002"><exercise id="_3b03d196-7526-4071-b198-999c2e4d4c08" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00001"><para id="para-00002">Match each equation with a verbal description that represents the same function.</para>
      <para id="para-00003"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem><solution id="sol-00001"><para id="para-00004">Correct!  To get the output, multiply the input by 2, then add 4 to the result.</para><para id="para-00005">Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.2.</para><para id="para-00006">The correct answer is to get the output, multiply the input by 2, then add 4 to the result.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_234da651-94df-4ff5-af49-007f3ed47257" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00002"><para id="para-00007"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem><solution id="sol-00002"><para id="para-00008">Correct!  To get the output, add 4 to the input, then multiply the result by 2.</para><para id="para-00009">Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.2.</para><para id="para-00010">The correct answer is To get the output, add 4 to the input, then multiply the result by 2 <emphasis>.</emphasis></para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="bf984679-4679-4e9b-bd3b-85ae0fd95e57" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00003"><para id="para-00011"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem><solution id="sol-00003"><para id="para-00012">Correct!  To get the output, multiply the input by 4, then add 2 to the result.</para><para id="para-00013">Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.2.</para><para id="para-00014">The correct answer is to get the output, multiply the input by 4, then add 2 to the result.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_5955ed6d-6f72-4398-bb5d-80cb2b9881a9" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00004"><para id="para-00015"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>k</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem><solution id="sol-00004"><para id="para-00016">Correct!  To get the output, add 2 to the input, then multiply the result by 4.</para><para id="para-00017">Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.2.</para><para id="para-00018">The correct answer is To get the output, add 2 to the input, then multiply the result by 4.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_0d08ce71-3fc2-4a8f-a27e-c97d363f1731" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00005"><para id="para-00019">Functions <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>A</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>B</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> are defined by these equations.
          <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>A</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>25</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>B</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>80</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>15</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> 
          Which function has a greater value when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is 2.5?</para>
      <para id="para-00020">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00021"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>A</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>25</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00022"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>B</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>80</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>15</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem><solution id="sol-00005"><para id="para-00023">Correct!  Function A has a greater value because B(2.5)=42.5 and A(2.5)=50.</para><para id="para-00024">Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.3.</para><para id="para-00025">The correct answer is Function A has a greater value because <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>B</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2.5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>42.5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>A</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2.5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>50</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_998043ad-68ac-4dc6-b932-88437166f755" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00006"><para id="para-00026">Which function is greater when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
      <para id="para-00027">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00028"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00029"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00030"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00031"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem><solution id="sol-00006"><para id="para-00032">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00033">Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.2.</para><para id="para-00034">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="a6cbad77-b6a6-46d6-9940-8b2019b175a9" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00007"><para id="para-00035">Which function rule describes the table below:</para>
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable" id="table-00001">
        <tgroup cols="6"><tbody><row>
            <entry><emphasis>
              <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>
           </emphasis> </entry><entry>
              2
            </entry>
            <entry>
              3
            </entry>
            <entry>
              4
            </entry>
            <entry>
              5
            </entry>
            <entry>
              6
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry><emphasis>
              <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>
           </emphasis> </entry><entry>
              3
            </entry>
            <entry>
              5
            </entry>
            <entry>
              7
            </entry>
            <entry>
              9
            </entry>
            <entry>
              11
            </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody></tgroup></table>
      
    <para id="para-00036">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00037"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00038"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00039"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00040"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem><solution id="sol-00007"><para id="para-00041">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00042">Try again. Revisit activities 4.4.3.</para><para id="para-00043">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_5ea74f7e-7211-4aa4-ae4f-db4b69b5ad08" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00008"><para id="para-00044">Write a function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> for the following statement: to get the output, subtract 4 from the input, then multiply the result by 2.</para>
      <para id="para-00045">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00046"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00047"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00048"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00049"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem><solution id="sol-00008"><para id="para-00050">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00051">Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.1.</para><para id="para-00052">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="ad08a7ed-c590-4281-852d-11570c6bce38" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00009"><para id="para-00053">Write a function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> for the following statement: to get the output, multiply the input by 5 and then add 2.</para>
      <para id="para-00054">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00055"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00056"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00057"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00058"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem><solution id="sol-00009"><para id="para-00059">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00060">Try again. Revisit activities 4.4.1.</para><para id="para-00061">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="c60f5cda-248c-45f1-b8d8-19fc43601821" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00010"><para id="para-00062">Find the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
      <para id="para-00063">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00064">7</para><para id="para-00065">1</para><para id="para-00066">-1</para><para id="para-00067">-7</para></problem><solution id="sol-00010"><para id="para-00068">Correct! -7</para><para id="para-00069">Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.2.</para><para id="para-00070">The correct answer is -7.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="e067d2ce-4e9a-4fe3-87c3-6fbb16068c95" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00011"><para id="para-00071">Examine the table below. Find <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2.5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> using the rule for this table.</para>
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable" id="table-00002">
        <tgroup cols="5"><tbody><row>
            <entry><emphasis>
              <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>
           </emphasis> </entry><entry>
              1
            </entry>
            <entry>
              2
            </entry>
            <entry>
              3
            </entry>
            <entry>
              4
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry><emphasis>
              <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>
           </emphasis> </entry><entry>
              2
            </entry>
            <entry>
              6
            </entry>
            <entry>
              10
            </entry>
            <entry>
              14
            </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody></tgroup></table>
      
    </problem><solution id="sol-00011"><para id="para-00072">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2.5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00073">Try again. Revisit activities 4.4.4.</para><para id="para-00074">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2.5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content></document>